   would report a PHANTOM drift on a branch that never touched that bundle's sources.

   Fix the disagreement, do not regenerate the bundle around it:
     • a direct dependency disagrees → pin the SAME exact version in package.json (root)
       and packages/core/package.json, then regenerate BOTH locks:
         npm install --package-lock-only
         cd packages/core && npm install --package-lock-only --no-workspaces
     • a transitive dependency disagrees → move the lagging lock to the other one's
       version (e.g. `npm update <pkg> --package-lock-only` in the lagging layer), then
       rebuild any bundle whose inlined bytes change
     • a world reports <absent> → that lock does not plan the package at all; add it
       where it is imported, or rebuild the bundle if it no longer inlines it
     • tree disagrees → re-install to lockfile state (CI parity):
         NODE_ENV=development npm install
